Define the preferences structure once

`prefs' is declared extern in galculator.h and DEFINED in both main.c and
config_file.c.  Two definitions of one object is not legal C; it linked for
years only because the compilers of the day defaulted to -fcommon, which
quietly merges tentative definitions of the same name into one.  GCC 10 made
-fno-common the default and the link now fails outright:

  multiple definition of `prefs'; galculator-main.o: first defined here

config_file.c is the one that has to keep it.  Its prefs_list[] table is a
static initialiser holding the address of every field -- &(prefs.bkg_color)
and fifty-two more -- so the object must be complete at file scope there.
main.c only ever reads and writes it through the extern declaration it already
gets from galculator.h, so its copy is redundant as well as illegal.

--- a/src/main.c
+++ b/src/main.c
@@ -49,7 +49,6 @@
 
 #define MASK_NUMLOCK GDK_MOD2_MASK
 
-s_preferences		prefs;
 s_current_status 	current_status = {0, 0, 0, 0, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE};
 s_array				memory;
 s_constant 			*constant;
